{"type":"excalidraw/clipboard","elements":[{"id":"_4JDiPsHybNXLp3E77G5J","type":"text","x":-5067.166929001238,"y":2971.661547761547,"width":1045.2,"height":37.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1616572959,"version":106,"versionNonce":1413350673,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Device Telemetry Platform  -  100 M agents, one snapshot every 30 s","originalText":"Device Telemetry Platform  -  100 M agents, one snapshot every 30 s","fontSize":30,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpS"},{"id":"hOMDNDfLkNma84VaQPuBC","type":"text","x":-5067.166929001238,"y":3017.661547761547,"width":924.5600000000001,"height":17.5,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":227890751,"version":106,"versionNonce":442323071,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"one write door, one queue in the middle, and every number the dashboard shows was already finished before anybody asked for it.","originalText":"one write door, one queue in the middle, and every number the dashboard shows was already finished before anybody asked for it.","fontSize":14,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpT"},{"id":"-EZOrow1NfSRzk7ZJOh9k","type":"rectangle","x":-5067.166929001238,"y":3061.661547761547,"width":860,"height":470,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1244542559,"version":106,"versionNonce":1094531825,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"roundness":{"type":3},"index":"bpU"},{"id":"pGoa3TYkGsvO3OIgDGezZ","type":"text","x":-5047.166929001238,"y":3077.661547761547,"width":265.2,"height":18.75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":485888639,"version":106,"versionNonce":1753016479,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"A.  FUNCTIONAL  -  what it must do","originalText":"A.  FUNCTIONAL  -  what it must do","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpV"},{"id":"Ln3NxAudccq71XpcysHNp","type":"text","x":-5045.166929001238,"y":3113.661547761547,"width":399.36,"height":315,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1588423327,"version":106,"versionNonce":412792017,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"1   every agent pushes one JSON snapshot every 30 seconds\n       battery, cpu, disk, uptime, firmware\n\n2   we accept it, or we tell it to slow down.\n       we never drop it in silence.\n\n3   every raw payload is kept, exactly as it arrived, for audit\n\n4   an admin opens ONE screen and sees the fleet right now\n       '20 % of devices are battery depleted'  -  and can slice\n       that by model, OS version, firmware and region\n\n5   an admin clicks a number and gets the devices behind it,\n       then the chart of any single one of them\n\n6   an admin writes rules  -  'battery under 10 % for 5 minutes'\n       -  and is paged ONCE, not two hundred thousand times\n\n7   an admin can pull raw payloads back for a date range\n\n8   nice to have: config push, firmware rollout tracking","originalText":"1   every agent pushes one JSON snapshot every 30 seconds\n       battery, cpu, disk, uptime, firmware\n\n2   we accept it, or we tell it to slow down.\n       we never drop it in silence.\n\n3   every raw payload is kept, exactly as it arrived, for audit\n\n4   an admin opens ONE screen and sees the fleet right now\n       '20 % of devices are battery depleted'  -  and can slice\n       that by model, OS version, firmware and region\n\n5   an admin clicks a number and gets the devices behind it,\n       then the chart of any single one of them\n\n6   an admin writes rules  -  'battery under 10 % for 5 minutes'\n       -  and is paged ONCE, not two hundred thousand times\n\n7   an admin can pull raw payloads back for a date range\n\n8   nice to have: config push, firmware rollout tracking","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpW"},{"id":"HAEpV12SgB6gq9FKGnY5i","type":"rectangle","x":-4167.166929001238,"y":3061.661547761547,"width":860,"height":470,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":2080685759,"version":106,"versionNonce":1530166463,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"roundness":{"type":3},"index":"bpX"},{"id":"5Fr_MefF_E2UnsqidBGNf","type":"text","x":-4147.166929001238,"y":3077.661547761547,"width":241.8,"height":18.75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":2006748895,"version":106,"versionNonce":2112746161,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"B.  NON FUNCTIONAL  -  how well","originalText":"B.  NON FUNCTIONAL  -  how well","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpY"},{"id":"vtbf1bXzp9o4upiBWQYtm","type":"text","x":-4145.166929001238,"y":3113.661547761547,"width":393.12,"height":360,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":738548479,"version":106,"versionNonce":371494111,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"1   CAP  -  there is no one answer here, there are four\n\n     INGEST                availability  >  consistency\n         a refused write becomes a retry, and 100 M retries is\n         a second outage on top of the first. take it, remember\n         it, sort it out afterwards.\n\n     DASHBOARD             availability  >  consistency\n         a count 10 s old is fine. a blank screen is not. but\n         every screen carries an 'as of' stamp, so stale data\n         never gets to pretend it is live.\n\n     AUDIT LAKE            durability first, speed last\n         we may lose a dashboard. we may not lose a payload.\n\n     RULES / ALERTS / AUTHZ    consistency  >  availability\n         two engines disagreeing about one firing alert pages a\n         human twice at 3 am. one Postgres, one truth.\n\n2   dashboard under 200 ms   |   event visible within 20 s\n     ingest answers in 30 ms  -  it only ever says 'got it'\n\n3   WRITE heavy  -  3 300 writes for every 1 read\n4   one broken device must not hurt the other 99 999 999","originalText":"1   CAP  -  there is no one answer here, there are four\n\n     INGEST                availability  >  consistency\n         a refused write becomes a retry, and 100 M retries is\n         a second outage on top of the first. take it, remember\n         it, sort it out afterwards.\n\n     DASHBOARD             availability  >  consistency\n         a count 10 s old is fine. a blank screen is not. but\n         every screen carries an 'as of' stamp, so stale data\n         never gets to pretend it is live.\n\n     AUDIT LAKE            durability first, speed last\n         we may lose a dashboard. we may not lose a payload.\n\n     RULES / ALERTS / AUTHZ    consistency  >  availability\n         two engines disagreeing about one firing alert pages a\n         human twice at 3 am. one Postgres, one truth.\n\n2   dashboard under 200 ms   |   event visible within 20 s\n     ingest answers in 30 ms  -  it only ever says 'got it'\n\n3   WRITE heavy  -  3 300 writes for every 1 read\n4   one broken device must not hurt the other 99 999 999","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpZ"},{"id":"CShn7ee8BpagEMVw_xg_U","type":"rectangle","x":-3267.166929001238,"y":3061.661547761547,"width":860,"height":470,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1304404767,"version":106,"versionNonce":903771281,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"roundness":{"type":3},"index":"bpa"},{"id":"M-xVCyyp4_xqCR7yMzXxN","type":"text","x":-3247.166929001238,"y":3077.661547761547,"width":312,"height":18.75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":758900543,"version":106,"versionNonce":1960679679,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"C.  ESTIMATION  -  the numbers you quote","originalText":"C.  ESTIMATION  -  the numbers you quote","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpb"},{"id":"kFcwYDEnTyYIv8TCF-X3Q","type":"text","x":-3245.166929001238,"y":3113.661547761547,"width":430.56,"height":330,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":953853791,"version":106,"versionNonce":69450353,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"devices        100 M agents, one snapshot every 30 s\n\nwrite rate     100 M / 30 s  =  3.3 M events / s  sustained\npeak           a reboot storm or a bad config push, 2 x = 6.6 M / s\n               this one number IS the design. all else follows.\n\npayload        ~800 bytes of JSON  ( ~250 bytes gzipped on the wire )\nevents / day   100 M x 2 880  =  288 BILLION events / day\n\nraw volume     288 B x 800 B  =  ~230 TB / day uncompressed\naudit lake     columnar + zstd ~15 x  =  ~15 TB / day  =  5.5 PB / yr\n               this line is why raw never goes near a database\n\nreads          ~5 000 admins, a tile every 5 s  =  ~1 K reads / s\nratio          3 300 : 1  WRITE heavy\n               ->  count on write, never scan on read\n\ncounters       a few hundred numbers per tenant, under 4 KB of Redis\nlatest state   ~200 B x 100 M  =  ~20 GB of Redis, sharded\nkafka          6.6 M/s x 800 B = ~5 GB/s peak, 5 000 partitions,\n               7 d retention = ~1.6 PB broker disk -> tiered to S3\ningest fleet   3.3 M rps / ~30 K rps a node = ~110 nodes, 3 regions","originalText":"devices        100 M agents, one snapshot every 30 s\n\nwrite rate     100 M / 30 s  =  3.3 M events / s  sustained\npeak           a reboot storm or a bad config push, 2 x = 6.6 M / s\n               this one number IS the design. all else follows.\n\npayload        ~800 bytes of JSON  ( ~250 bytes gzipped on the wire )\nevents / day   100 M x 2 880  =  288 BILLION events / day\n\nraw volume     288 B x 800 B  =  ~230 TB / day uncompressed\naudit lake     columnar + zstd ~15 x  =  ~15 TB / day  =  5.5 PB / yr\n               this line is why raw never goes near a database\n\nreads          ~5 000 admins, a tile every 5 s  =  ~1 K reads / s\nratio          3 300 : 1  WRITE heavy\n               ->  count on write, never scan on read\n\ncounters       a few hundred numbers per tenant, under 4 KB of Redis\nlatest state   ~200 B x 100 M  =  ~20 GB of Redis, sharded\nkafka          6.6 M/s x 800 B = ~5 GB/s peak, 5 000 partitions,\n               7 d retention = ~1.6 PB broker disk -> tiered to S3\ningest fleet   3.3 M rps / ~30 K rps a node = ~110 nodes, 3 regions","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpc"},{"id":"gtBVQeResHqS0SqokoCgR","type":"rectangle","x":-5067.166929001238,"y":3561.661547761547,"width":860,"height":410,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1055679359,"version":106,"versionNonce":216015135,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"roundness":{"type":3},"index":"bpd"},{"id":"9tchx0jjsKZQVWLJdcrZU","type":"text","x":-5047.166929001238,"y":3577.661547761547,"width":132.6,"height":18.75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1873910687,"version":106,"versionNonce":1233470545,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"D.  CORE ENTITIES","originalText":"D.  CORE ENTITIES","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpe"},{"id":"rK5gSPolYpMeUo_hqoOF7","type":"text","x":-5045.166929001238,"y":3613.661547761547,"width":418.08000000000004,"height":330,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":526045119,"version":106,"versionNonce":1872536895,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Device        deviceId | tenantId | model | osVersion | firmware\n              | registeredAt\n\nSnapshot      eventId | deviceId | seq | emittedAt | receivedAt\n              | schemaVersion | battery | cpu | disk | uptime\n                  eventId  =  the repeat key\n                  seq      =  the ordering key\n                  two clocks on purpose:  theirs and ours\n\nDeviceState   deviceId | lastSeenAt | values | bucket\n                  one row per device, overwritten in place\n\nFleetCount    tenantId | dimension | bucket | count\nRollupRow     tenantId | minute | model | osVersion | region\n              | bucket | count\n\nAlertRule     id | tenantId | expression | threshold | forDuration\nAlertInstance id | ruleId | fingerprint | state | startedAt | count\n                  state:  ok -> pending -> firing -> resolved\n\nAuditBlob     blobKey | tenantId | minTs | maxTs | rows | sha256\nAdmin         id | tenantId | role      viewer | operator | owner","originalText":"Device        deviceId | tenantId | model | osVersion | firmware\n              | registeredAt\n\nSnapshot      eventId | deviceId | seq | emittedAt | receivedAt\n              | schemaVersion | battery | cpu | disk | uptime\n                  eventId  =  the repeat key\n                  seq      =  the ordering key\n                  two clocks on purpose:  theirs and ours\n\nDeviceState   deviceId | lastSeenAt | values | bucket\n                  one row per device, overwritten in place\n\nFleetCount    tenantId | dimension | bucket | count\nRollupRow     tenantId | minute | model | osVersion | region\n              | bucket | count\n\nAlertRule     id | tenantId | expression | threshold | forDuration\nAlertInstance id | ruleId | fingerprint | state | startedAt | count\n                  state:  ok -> pending -> firing -> resolved\n\nAuditBlob     blobKey | tenantId | minTs | maxTs | rows | sha256\nAdmin         id | tenantId | role      viewer | operator | owner","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpf"},{"id":"M-GdXkiE9vFvsqdt0XPEN","type":"rectangle","x":-4167.166929001238,"y":3561.661547761547,"width":860,"height":410,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1208516575,"version":106,"versionNonce":1641714225,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"roundness":{"type":3},"index":"bpg"},{"id":"ih4AzvhpXg5b5nmjRmyla","type":"text","x":-4147.166929001238,"y":3577.661547761547,"width":109.2,"height":18.75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1271606271,"version":106,"versionNonce":745776479,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"E.  API DESIGN","originalText":"E.  API DESIGN","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bph"},{"id":"eCJVsWCpHxQ8wA0DxwTDY","type":"text","x":-4145.166929001238,"y":3613.661547761547,"width":405.6,"height":315,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1990415391,"version":106,"versionNonce":1108026385,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"INGEST\nPOST /v1/telemetry\n     headers: x-api-key, x-device-id, x-idempotency-key\n     body    { eventId, seq, emittedAt, metrics { ... } }\n     202     { ackedUpTo, nextPushAfterSec, backoffHint }\n     429     Retry-After: 60     the agent is TOLD to slow down\nGET  /v1/agent/manifest      what to send, how often  ->  the CDN\n\nDASHBOARD\nGET  /v1/fleet/summary?window=1m\n                          ->  { total, byBucket { ... }, asOf }\nGET  /v1/fleet/breakdown?groupBy=model&metric=battery\nGET  /v1/devices?filter=battery<10&cursor=&limit=50\nGET  /v1/devices/{id}/series?metric=cpu&from=&to=&step=1m\nWS   /v1/stream?since=<seq>   resumes from that sequence\nGET  /v1/audit/export?from=&to=&deviceId=\n                          ->  a signed link, never the bytes\n\nALERTS\nPOST /v1/alert-rules   |   GET /v1/alerts?state=firing\nPOST /v1/alerts/{id}/ack","originalText":"INGEST\nPOST /v1/telemetry\n     headers: x-api-key, x-device-id, x-idempotency-key\n     body    { eventId, seq, emittedAt, metrics { ... } }\n     202     { ackedUpTo, nextPushAfterSec, backoffHint }\n     429     Retry-After: 60     the agent is TOLD to slow down\nGET  /v1/agent/manifest      what to send, how often  ->  the CDN\n\nDASHBOARD\nGET  /v1/fleet/summary?window=1m\n                          ->  { total, byBucket { ... }, asOf }\nGET  /v1/fleet/breakdown?groupBy=model&metric=battery\nGET  /v1/devices?filter=battery<10&cursor=&limit=50\nGET  /v1/devices/{id}/series?metric=cpu&from=&to=&step=1m\nWS   /v1/stream?since=<seq>   resumes from that sequence\nGET  /v1/audit/export?from=&to=&deviceId=\n                          ->  a signed link, never the bytes\n\nALERTS\nPOST /v1/alert-rules   |   GET /v1/alerts?state=firing\nPOST /v1/alerts/{id}/ack","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpi"},{"id":"0CMrKOqqRMksI_g65vAyG","type":"rectangle","x":-3267.166929001238,"y":3561.661547761547,"width":860,"height":450,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"dashed","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1082226751,"version":106,"versionNonce":313893247,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"roundness":{"type":3},"index":"bpj"},{"id":"ZRHoE-C2UQZnviGdqYf7b","type":"text","x":-3247.166929001238,"y":3577.661547761547,"width":210.6,"height":18.75,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":1329993823,"version":106,"versionNonce":1443789297,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"F.  WHY EACH PIECE IS THERE","originalText":"F.  WHY EACH PIECE IS THERE","fontSize":15,"fontFamily":6,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"autoResize":true,"lineHeight":1.25,"roundness":null,"index":"bpk"},{"id":"V5QYvBCv483OHjAQwjr1x","type":"text","x":-3245.166929001238,"y":3613.661547761547,"width":430.56,"height":360,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e1e1e","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":1,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":1,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"seed":952218751,"version":106,"versionNonce":866326943,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1787459983943,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"Kafka           the shock absorber. ingest answers in 30 ms because\n                NOTHING downstream is in the request path, and 7 days\n                of retention means a broken consumer replays instead\n                of losing data.\n\nRedis counters  the only thing that answers '20 % of 100 M' in 1 ms.\n\nClickHouse      every slice an admin might ask for, already counted,\n                per minute. a column store, so no index is needed.\n\nCassandra       one device's history - one partition, newest first,\n                never a scan.\n\nS3 + lock       the audit answer. written once, cannot be edited,\n                cheap after 30 days.\n\nPostgres        the small exact things: who a device belongs to, who\n                may see it, whether an alert is firing. the only\n                place we need a transaction.\n\nCDN             100 M agents polling config must never reach us.\n\nRedis Streams   the last 5 minutes of updates, so a reconnecting\n                browser catches up instead of reloading the world.","originalText":"Kafka           the shock absorber. ingest answers in 30 ms because\n                NOTHING downstream is in the request path, and 7 days\n                of retention means a broken consumer replays instead\n                of losing data.\n\nRedis counters  the only thing that answers '20 % of 100 M' in 1 ms.\n\nClickHouse      every slice an admin might ask for, already counted,\n                per minute. a column store, so no index is needed.\n\nCassandra       one device's history - one partition, newest first,\n                never a scan.\n\nS3 + lock       the audit answer. written once, cannot be edited,\n                cheap after 30 days.\n\nPostgres        the small exact things: who a device belongs to, who\n                may see it, whether an alert is firing. the only\n                place we need a transaction.\n\nCDN             100 M agents polling config must never reach us.\n\nRedis Streams   the last 5 minutes of updates, so a reconnecting\n                browser catches up instead of reloading the world.","fontSize":12,"fontFamily":6,